# A phrasal verb is a verb plus a short word such as `up`, `out`, or
# `off` that together act as one verb (`set up`, `look up`). An
# idiomatic one means something its words do not add up to (`figure
# out`, `kick off`, `get rid of`). A reader who does not know the idiom
# cannot parse it, and a dictionary lookup of each word fails. Each
# phrase here has a one-word verb that says the same thing: find, learn,
# write, become, start, create, send, remove, examine, meet, show, read,
# exclude, fix, connect, stop, review, wait, assemble, track, handle,
# watch, apply, retire, exit, or locate. `go ahead and` adds nothing, so
# the fix deletes it.
#
# Phrases that docs use as technical terms or in their literal sense
# stay out: `fall back` (`fallback`), `go through` (`the request goes
# through the proxy`), `make up`, `leave out`, `lay out`, `carry
# over`, and `call out` (`calls out to a subprocess`). The Optional
# rule of the same name holds `set up`, `clean up`, `show up`, and
# `turn into`, which docs use often and mostly read one way.
#
# Each verb lists its forms by hand, irregular ones included (`found`,
# `brought`, `dug`).
expr main [([find, finds, found, finding] out), ([figure, figures, figured, figuring] out), ([come, comes, came, coming] up with), ([end, ends, ended, ending] up), ([kick, kicks, kicked, kicking] off), ([spin, spins, spun, spinning] up), ([bring, brings, brought, bringing] up), ([fire, fires, fired, firing] off), ([get, gets, got, gotten, getting] rid of), ([look, looks, looked, looking] into), ([come, comes, came, coming] across), ([run, runs, ran, running] into), ([point, points, pointed, pointing] out), ([pick, picks, picked, picking] up), ([weed, weeds, weeded, weeding] out), ([boil, boils, boiled, boiling] down), ([rule, rules, ruled, ruling] out), ([sort, sorts, sorted, sorting] out), ([dig, digs, dug, digging] into), ([wire, wires, wired, wiring] up), ([hook, hooks, hooked, hooking] up), ([give, gives, gave, given, giving] up), ([go, goes, went, gone, going] over), ([hold, holds, held, holding] off), ([put, puts, putting] together), ([keep, keeps, kept, keeping] track of), ([take, takes, took, taken, taking] care of), ([deal, deals, dealt, dealing] with), ([keep, keeps, kept, keeping] an eye on), ([go, goes, went, going] ahead and), ([come, comes, came, coming] into play), ([iron, irons, ironed, ironing] out), ([phase, phases, phased, phasing] out), ([bail, bails, bailed, bailing] out), ([zero, zeroes, zeros, zeroed, zeroing] in on)]
let message "Phrasal verb. Use one verb, such as find, start, or remove."
let description "Flags idiomatic phrasal verbs, such as figure out and kick off, that one plain verb replaces."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The finder returns the first match."
allows "The request goes through the proxy."
allows "The client falls back to the default."
allows "The end of the list holds the newest entry."
